    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-capital-territory-evidence-temporary-provisions-act-1971-sec-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Validation of provisions of Australian Capital Territory Evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-capital-territory-evidence-temporary-provisions-act-1971#sec-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-capital-territory-evidence-temporary-provisions-act-1971.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-evidence-temporary-provisions-act-1971.pdf, p.5",
      "values:originalText": "Ordinance\n\n(1) The provisions of the Australian Capital Territory Evidence\nOrdinance 1971 contained in Australian Capital Territory\nOrdinance No. 4 of 1971 shall, notwithstanding its disallowance by\nthe Senate, continue in force.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) prevents the amendment or repeal by an\nOrdinance under the Seat of Government (Administration) Act\n1910 of the provisions continued in force by that subsection.\n\n(3) The Interpretation Ordinance 1967 of the Australian Capital\nTerritory, as amended and in force from time to time, applies, and\nshall be deemed to have always applied, to the provisions\ncontinued in force by subsection (1).\n\n\nEndnotes\n\nEndnote 1—Legislation history\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971\n\nEndnotes\n\nEndnote 1—Legislation history\nThis endnote sets out details of the legislation history of the Australian Capital\nTerritory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971.\n\nAct\nNumber\nand year\nAssent\nCommencement\nApplication,\nsaving and\ntransitional\nprovisions\nAustralian Capital\nTerritory Evidence\n(Temporary Provisions)\nAct 1971\n66, 1971",
      "skos:definition": "Ordinance\n\n(1) The provisions of the Australian Capital Territory Evidence\nOrdinance 1971 contained in Australian Capital Territory\nOrdinance No. 4 of 1971 shall, notwithstanding its disallowance by\nthe Senate, continue in force.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) prevents the amendment or repeal by an\nOrdinance under the Seat of Government (Administration) Act\n1910 of the provisions continued in force by that subsection.\n\n(3) The Interpretation Ordinance 1967 of the Australian Capital\nTerritory, as amended and in force from time to time, applies, and\nshall be deemed to have always applied, to the provisions\ncontinued in force by subsection (1).\n\n\nEndnotes\n\nEndnote 1—Legislation history\n\nAustralian Capital Territory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971\n\nEndnotes\n\nEndnote 1—Legislation history\nThis endnote sets out details of the legislation history of the Australian Capital\nTerritory Evidence (Temporary Provisions) Act 1971.\n\nAct\nNumber\nand year\nAssent\nCommencement\nApplication,\nsaving and\ntransitional\nprovisions\nAustralian Capital\nTerritory Evidence\n(Temporary Provisions)\nAct 1971\n66, 1971",
      "cml:hasPart": [
